From e47752fc1370862bc1e3b4e5a3a61df8771972aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:27:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] Vulkan: keep render passes open across draws;
 double-buffered batches

With VK_DRAW_BATCH=1:
- Consecutive draws into the same framebuffer that sample none of its
  images continue one render pass instead of each ending it behind a
  full barrier; clears, copies, uploads and flushes close it first.
- A batch flush submits without waiting and swaps in a second ring set,
  descriptor pool, command buffer and fence, so the walker records the
  next batch while the GPU runs this one. Anything that needs all GPU
  work complete (destroys, readbacks, unbatched work) waits for it
  (vk_eng_flush_sync); VK_DRAW_BATCH_SYNC=1 keeps the old behaviour.
- The per-frame colour snapshot is recorded into the batch.

3D Dot Game Heroes gameplay: ~14 -> ~17.5 flips/s on RADV Renoir.
VK_WAIT_STATS=1 reports synchronous waits by call site.
